        <body>
            <div xml:id="d977">

                <pb facs="0901" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/7191.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of
                        War.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-04-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 25, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith, for
                    such action as may be deemed appropriate, a translation of a note from the
                    Chargé d’Affaires of Mexico, in which he requests that General Ojeda, and the
                    persons who accompanied him when he entered the United States after the recent
                    battle at Naco, Sonora, be allowed to return to Mexico.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d977-a1.xml" xpointer="d977-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
